{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#1177","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#1177","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#1177\",\"parent_revision\":\"34e432f565f105dcf8fec0ea6e0c171efa1dfdbdfe62c3b1bc26041bcc772999\",\"root_revision\":\"34e432f565f105dcf8fec0ea6e0c171efa1dfdbdfe62c3b1bc26041bcc772999\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P2\\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-12\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nThe development harness documents IssueBackend and TaskBackend as planned Protocols in docs/backend-providers.md, but neither exists as formal Python code. The BacklogItem YAML schema (introduced in P964) was not designed against a backend-agnostic interface \u2014 several fields have no equivalent on GitLab or Linear: last_synced (models GitHub-as-canonical / local-cache pattern), groomed, research_first, files, and suggested_location (local annotations with no backend primitive on any platform). github_sync.py operates below the abstraction layer and conforms to no formal Protocol. Until IssueBackend is defined in Python and BacklogItem fields are audited for portability, building GitLab or Linear adapters has no specified contract to follow and risks per-adapter field mapping decisions made ad-hoc.\\n\\nVerbatim user report: 'Yes, if there isn't one already then yes i do want a backlog item to formalize it'\\n\\n## RT-ICA\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAssessment date: 2026-04-23\\n\\n| # | Condition | Status | Source |\\n|---|-----------|--------|--------|\\n| 1 | IssueBackend methods derivable from github_sync.py | AVAILABLE \u2014 `github_sync.py` is the only current backend; its public methods define the de-facto interface |\\n| 2 | BacklogItem fields | AVAILABLE \u2014 listed in issue description: `last_synced`, `groomed`, `research_first`, `files`, `suggested_location` as GitHub-only/local-annotation |\\n| 3 | GitLab/Linear field equivalents | DERIVABLE \u2014 requires GitLab Issues API and Linear GraphQL API docs; both are publicly documented |\\n| 4 | docs/backend-providers.md exists | AVAILABLE \u2014 referenced in issue description as existing planned documentation |\\n| 5 | Protocol placement in codebase | DERIVABLE \u2014 `backlog_core/protocols.py` follows existing module naming conventions |\\n| 6 | Whether `BacklogItem` schema (#964) was designed for portability | AVAILABLE \u2014 issue confirms it was NOT designed against backend-agnostic interface |\\n\\nVerdict: READY \u2014 core interface is DERIVABLE from existing code. External API research needed for GitLab/Linear field mappings but is standard documentation research.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-04-23)\\n\\n### Impact\\n\\nP2 Feature. 3 existing files updated + 1 new file. No runtime behavior change \u2014 Protocol is a type-checking construct. Enables correct GitLab/Linear adapter development. Strengthens type system \u2014 aligns with repo typing improvement directive.\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n- [ ] `IssueBackend` Protocol defined in Python (e.g., `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/protocols.py`) with all methods required to support CRUD on backlog items\\n- [ ] `TaskBackend` Protocol defined if documented in `docs/backend-providers.md` alongside `IssueBackend`\\n- [ ] `BacklogItem` fields audited and each field tagged as: `universal` | `github-only` | `local-annotation` | `derivable-on-other-backends`\\n- [ ] Fields with no primitive on GitLab or Linear documented with migration strategy (e.g., store in issue description as structured block)\\n- [ ] `github_sync.py` updated or annotated to indicate which `IssueBackend` methods it implements\\n- [ ] `docs/backend-providers.md` updated to reference the formal Protocol definition instead of planned-only documentation\\n\\n### Files\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/protocols.py` \u2014 new file: `IssueBackend` Protocol definition\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/github_sync.py` \u2014 annotate/type to conform to Protocol\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/models.py` \u2014 `BacklogItem` field portability tags\\n- `plugins/development-harness/docs/backend-providers.md` \u2014 update planned \u2192 formal Protocol reference\\n\\n### Story\\n\\nAs a developer building backend adapters (GitLab, Linear) for the development harness, I need a formal Python `IssueBackend` Protocol and a BacklogItem field portability audit so that adapters have a specified contract to implement rather than ad-hoc field mappings.\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer using Claude Code skills**, I want to **formalise issuebackend protocol and audit backlogitem field portability across backends** so that **the tooling becomes more capable and complete**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Session observation \u2014 discovered during P964 backlog-yaml-migration QG audit (2026-03-30)\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-03-30\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"e682e972a7200f3cb7c917afa2a3d81d01ce95a5e4a1b099bb09757c14376f09\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPS9GhQ\"}"}